<title>USA: Bangor Hydro Q1 shr $0.05 vs $0.51.</title>
<headline>Bangor Hydro Q1 shr $0.05 vs $0.51.</headline>
<dateline>BANGOR, Maine 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months ended March 31:	     1997	     1996</p>
<p> Revenues				 $183,801,362   $184,811,214</p>
<p> Net Income				  7,903,458	5,138,543</p>
<p> Earnings per Common Share		     .87		.47</p>
<p> Weighted Average Number of Shares   7,348,850	7,287,181</p>
<p> Three months ended March 31:		1997	     1996</p>
<p> Revenues				   48,175,751     48,160,720</p>
<p> Net Income				    716,121	4,095,330</p>
<p> Earnings per Common Share		     .05		.51</p>
<p> Weighted Average Number of Shares   7,363,424	7,312,282</p>
<p>Bangor Hydro-Electric Company is the second largest</p>
<p>electric utility in Maine.</p>
<p>The company said the decline in first quarter earnings is connected to the shut-down of the Maine Yankee nuclear power plant, in which it has a seven percent interest.</p>
<p>The company said the plant was shut down in December 1996.</p>
</text>
